#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096326 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using the Chain and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "74ffb6be-e709-5635-b6e2-98911c40a19e" :question/math-academy-id "e-184" :question/problem "Given that $y =\\dfrac{e^{3x}}{2^{x}+1}$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=e^{3x}$ and the denominator\n\n$$\nv(x)=2^x +1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x)$, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x) = 3e^{3x}, \\qquad v'(x) = 2^x \\ln 2\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u$.\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} &= \\dfrac{u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x)\\cdot v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{3e^{3x} \\cdot \\left(2^{x}+1\\right) - e^{3x} \\cdot \\left(2^x \\cdot \\ln2\\right)}{\\left(2^{x}+1 \\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{3e^{3x}2^{x} + 3e^{3x} - e^{3x}2^{x}\\ln 2}{\\left(2^{x}+1 \\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\dfrac{e^{3x} \\left(3(2^{x}) - 2^{x} \\ln 2 +3\\right)}{\\left(2^{x}+1 \\right)^2} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096327 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using the Chain and Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "a2bb6a33-8a57-5b6b-9d35-cf611fbd5c9b" :question/math-academy-id "e-185" :question/problem "If $f(x) = e^{-2x}\\tan({x^2})$, then what is $f'(x)$?" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let\n\n$$\nu(x) = e^{-2x}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nv(x)=\\tan{(x^2)}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\nu'(x) = -2e^{-2x}, \\qquad v'(x) = 2x\\sec^2(x^2)\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to calculate both $u'(x)$ and $v'(x)$.\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= u^{′}(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v^{′}(x) \\\\\n&= (-2e^{-2x}) \\cdot \\tan (x^{2}) + e^{-2x} \\cdot 2x\\sec^{2} (x^{2}) \\\\\n&= 2e^{-2x}(-\\tan (x^{2}) + x\\sec^{2} (x^{2})) \\\\\n&= 2e^{-2x}(x\\sec^{2} (x^{2}) - \\tan (x^{2}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096463 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using Multiple Instances of the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "b00f1213-cdaf-512c-9842-92cbee1ec63a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6100" :question/problem "Differentiate $y = \\cos^4{2x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as a composite function\n\n$$\ny = u^4, \\qquad u = \\cos{v}, \\qquad v = 2x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = 4u^3,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d v} = -\\sin{v},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm d x} = 2\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{dy}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= \\frac{dy}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dv} \\cdot \\frac{dv}{dx} \\\\\n&= 4u^{3} \\cdot (-\\sin v) \\cdot (2) \\\\\n&= 4(\\cos 2x)^{3} \\cdot (-\\sin 2x) \\cdot (2) \\\\\n&=-8\\cos^{3} 2x\\sin 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using the Chain and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dcf0751-f342-57ee-88f5-7ab04150fb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x)/((3x + 5)^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094083} {:answer/id #uuid "be64dd14-3ea1-544b-93f1-d27c028793ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x)/((3x + 5)^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094084} {:answer/id #uuid "c47e1a10-0bcb-5123-8b30-228dd01ee56d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5x)/((3x + 5)^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094085} {:answer/id #uuid "10ec327f-9b94-56da-9c7c-e97d2c86f0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(30x)/((3x + 5)^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094086} {:answer/id #uuid "4df11836-1664-5e47-ba48-93d52815bd1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x)/((3x + 5)^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ec327f-9b94-56da-9c7c-e97d2c86f0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(30x)/((3x + 5)^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094086} :answer-field/id #uuid "a17443b5-e03a-52af-a8f8-80174508b99f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094082}] :question/id #uuid "4603accf-ccdb-5030-90b8-c9b568c4df0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11973" :question/problem "Given that $y = (3x^{2})/((3x + 5)^{2})$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using the Chain and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980aecfb-183b-5fea-a534-a74eef4c3965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) - \\tan (7x - 2))/(16x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095077} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b54e6c-32bd-5c6a-9dbd-a211d0225b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7x\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) - \\tan (7x - 2))/(16x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095078} {:answer/id #uuid "e768b7a0-f83f-5d0b-80dd-898cdf867862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) - \\tan (7x - 2))/(4x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095079} {:answer/id #uuid "3bda0a1f-ba43-5bc2-b4c6-f603bdb9d760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7x\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) - \\tan (7x - 2))/(4x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095080} {:answer/id #uuid "3f828d78-a786-5edd-b326-6e3442a41b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) + \\tan (7x - 2))/(4x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bda0a1f-ba43-5bc2-b4c6-f603bdb9d760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7x\\sec^{2} (7x - 2) - \\tan (7x - 2))/(4x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095080} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8fcf880-e9ed-53c6-b887-3e0063f1c7bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095076}] :question/id #uuid "3cae07ba-0147-5b66-85db-519e500d15f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-2396" :question/problem "Find $y^{′}$ for $y = (\\tan (7x - 2))/(4x)$."}]}
